.TH DPRIMEHOSTCACHE 8
.SH NAME
dprimehostcache \- dump or rebuild Diablo's incoming host cache
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dprimehostcache
.B \-dump
|
.B \-prime
[
.I hostcache
[
.I diablo.hosts
]
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
diablo decides which dnewsfeeds label an incoming connection belongs to
through a host cache, dhosts.cache in path_db.  It is built from the
host names and addresses in dnewsfeeds (alias, inhost) and, if it
exists, from the older diablo.hosts file, with their DNS lookups done
ahead of time.  diablo rebuilds it on its own when dnewsfeeds or
diablo.hosts change.
.PP
.B \-dump
prints the cache: one line per address with its host name and label.
.B \-prime
rebuilds the cache now, for example after a DNS change for a peer.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-dump
Print the contents of the host cache.
.TP
.B \-prime
Rebuild the host cache.
.TP
.I hostcache
Use this cache file instead of dhosts.cache.
.TP
.I diablo.hosts
Use this hosts file instead of diablo.hosts.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH BUGS
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
is read, but then also taken as the
.I hostcache
and
.I diablo.hosts
arguments.  Use DIABLO_CONFIG_PATH instead.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
diablo(8),
dnewsfeeds in diablo-files(5)
